{
    "title": "1922 GE AOU Fan Power cord Replacement",
    "last_updated": "August 9, 2019",
    "estimated_time": "15 minutes",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "introduction": "Use this guide to replace the power cord on a 1922 GE AOU fan.",
    "parts": [
        {
            "name": "Cloth Wire Power Cord",
            "url": "http://vintagewireandsupply.com/custom-cordset/",
            "for_sale_from_another_site": true,
            "view_link": "http://vintagewireandsupply.com/custom-cordset/"
        }
    ],
    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "6‑in-1 Screwdriver",
            "url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver",
            "image": "https://cart-products.cdn.ifixit.com/cart-products/LYcK13TjejldWD5Y.thumbnail",
            "price": "$6.99",
            "add_to_cart_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/products/6-in-1-screwdriver"
        }
    ],
    "steps": [
        {
            "step_number": 1,
            "title": "Power cord",
            "content": [
                "Tip the fan to its side and remove the three size 8 screws using a 9/32 flat-head screwdriver.",
                "The screws may be brittle from age, so be careful.",
                "Take the bottom plate off the fan and set it aside."
            ],
            "images": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HfEWGEh4CNaAfPT2.medium",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LZBxgpCDMiCQUKVN.medium"
            ],
            "images_200x150": [
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HfEWGEh4CNaAfPT2.200x150",
                "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/LZBxgpCDMiCQUKVN.200x150"
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134256",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 2,
            "content": [
                "Remove the three number 8 screws that hold the switch in place."
            ],
            "image": "https://guide-images.cdn.ifixit.com/igi/HTMJXZZZCcdmT1Rc.medium",
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134257",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 3,
            "content": [
                "Remove the switch, carefully sliding the speed lever out of its slot.",
                "Don't remove the switch too quickly or you can damage the head-wire."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134258",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 4,
            "content": [
                "Once the switch is free, unscrew the two knurled nuts holding the wires in place."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134260",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 5,
            "content": [
                "Turn the switch over and unscrew the nut securing the wire with the 5/16 crescent wrench."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134261",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        },
        {
            "step_number": 6,
            "content": [
                "Remove the switch and set it aside, then pull the wire through the grommet."
            ],
            "edit_url": "https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/edit/64228/134262",
            "comments_count": 0,
            "add_comment_url": null
        }
    ],
    "conclusion": "To reassemble your device, follow these instructions in reverse order.",
